result.notes:
Commit 264eef2f on story-364-architecture-as-built (unpushed). Items 1-3 done, docs and tests only, no production code.

ITEM 1, ARCHITECTURE.md. Status line no longer names a blueprint. how-brokkr-works' opening is merged into the intro and says journal events are hash-chained and unsigned (decision 0008); the guide now points at ARCHITECTURE and its duplicate deep-dive line is gone. Crate drawing now has every [dependencies] edge between workspace crates (added cli->core/store/protocol and bridge->core) and the sentence says so. Bridge is called the Looper dispatch bridge. LaneTally is added to the harness list (drawing and driver prose). Verb list removed, CLI reference linked. New short section: triage, the council, the dialect and the SDD route (0041/0042). Crossing named (0057). Re-graded against the code: the verify row was already correct at f4623a73 (verify gate under namespace hands; review seat is unboxed claude under the operator's permissions, per recipes/verify/bundle.json), so it is unchanged. Found and fixed one more stale claim: brokkr-view also depends on unicode-width (crates/brokkr-view/Cargo.toml). WORD CAP: DROPPED, not lowered. The page is 2,251 words (wc -w), because the SDD section and merged opening outweigh the removed verb list. The test is renamed the_architecture_page_is_pictures_first and keeps its diagram-count and front-page asserts.

ITEM 2, tests in crates/brokkr-cli/tests/diagrams.rs:
- crate test now also refuses a declared dependency left undrawn;
- the_effect_lifecycle_draws_every_effect_event: types from every event-envelope.v*.schema.json, parsed into brokkr_core::EventType, classified by a wildcard-free match; every effect/* type must be drawn;
- the_driver_sequence_draws_every_protocol_message: every driver-protocol.v* message family against E<->D arrows;
- the_policy_diagram_names_every_engine_owned_input: core's ENGINE_OWNED_INPUTS plus VISIT_PREFIX. There is no single INPUTS table on main (#345 has not landed), so I took ENGINE_OWNED_INPUTS as it.
Removal controls, all observed failing, then restored:
- bridge->core edge removed;
- effect/failed label removed;
- shutdown arrow removed;
- strategy removed from the label;
- planted driver-protocol.v2 with a 'pause' message;
- planted event-envelope.v2 with effect/retried ('core does not know');
- EffectFailed moved off the drawing ('effect/failed is an effect event...');
- RunParked moved off the drawing;
- '[dependencies] # planted' in the seatbelt-probe manifest ('header is unreadable').
Exact texts are in the commit message. A new core EventType variant fails to compile at the match by Rust exhaustiveness. I did not demonstrate that, because brokkr-view's own exhaustive matches break first.

ITEM 3. git mv to docs/history/. Each page gets a 'Historical' banner with a superseded-by table, and the blueprint also lists what is still wanted. Bodies, sections and status lines are kept. Relative links are fixed. Still-true extension-model parts (protected phase, seat ids, composition) are folded into recipe-authoring's new 'Adding a phase or a seat'. contributing.rs inventory rows for both are removed, and the ARCHITECTURE row's status line is updated. docs/history/ is added to support/records.rs and status_pages RECORDS. rename_guard FIXED_PROSE drops the two pages. Decision 0003's link target is updated to the new path (only that link changed).

RULING ASKS: (a) I KEPT the two blueprint rows in the_boundary_guides_keep_every_section_and_gained_the_rows, re-pathed, because the living spec openspec/specs/boundary-guides requires 'each page keeps every section and its status line'. That spec still names the old paths; a spec delta to re-path or retire that scenario is a follow-up. (b) Dropping the word cap rather than lowering it.

GATES, run here:
- cargo test -p brokkr-cli (all targets): it 520 passed, lib 627 passed, others green;
- cargo test -p brokkr-core: green;
- fmt --check clean;
- clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -D warnings clean;
- typos --hidden clean;
- lychee --offline --include-fragments on the changed and front pages: 0 errors;
- ratchet.sh files, clones and api hold;
- recipes/self and recipes/verify compile;
- git diff --check clean.
PENDING: mermaid-cli rendering. npm ci for .github/lint needed approval this seat lacks, so the four edited diagrams are unrendered locally; CI's non-Rust lints job renders them. Exact coverage is the controller's. Lychee was run on the changed pages, not over the whole tree.

FOLLOW-UPS: the openspec boundary-guides re-path; status_pages.rs keeps its own RECORDS list beside support/records.rs (pre-existing duplicate, ruling 5).

ITEM 4, ready-to-file issues (each: title / three-line body):
1) 'Signed checkpoints and a signed final receipt for the journal' / The journal is hash-chained and unkeyed; decision 0008 defers signing. / A verified chain catches a stale edit, not a recomputed rewrite or the author. / Wanted: operator-key signed checkpoints and receipt, verified by verify-run offline.
2) 'A content-addressed artifact store for prompts, transcripts, patches and logs' / The blueprint put large evidence in a digest-addressed directory beside the journal. / Today evidence is inline or in harness-owned files outside the run's export. / Wanted: digest, media type, size, producer and retention per artifact, checked by verify-run.
3) 'Cost, stagnation and elapsed-time budgets under decision 0067' / Seats are bounded only by max_attempts and timeout_seconds. / The blueprint asked every loop to declare cost, elapsed and stagnation limits, extendable by a journaled command. / Wanted: budgets as plan data per 0067, each exhaustion a typed park.
4) 'Container and remote runners for forge-driver/v1' / 0046's container boundary refuses at start until slice (iii); no remote transport exists. / Both were blueprint runners, and the deferred remote transport question is still open. / Wanted: the measured container boundary, then a remote transport that keeps the journal authoritative.
5) 'Compile-time liveness: prove every run can reach a terminal' / Compile proves the protected phase is unavoidable, and 0050's loader refuses dead rules, unreachable phases and dead ends. / It does not prove every bounded return loop exits. / Wanted: a liveness check over visit bounds, reported at compile, scoped after 0050's enactment.
